 "interpretation": "Chance AUC-PR = prevalence 0.378. Frozen pretrained DINOv2 (trained on clean) is far more robust than the from-scratch CNN to VIEWPOINT shift (0.632->0.615 vs 0.597->0.519) and to PHOTOMETRIC shift (surface tones + light; 0.632->0.562 vs 0.597->0.428), but MORE fragile to SENSOR degradation (noise 0.06 + gamma 1.5 + 3x3 blur on 48 px frames; 0.632->0.505 vs 0.597->0.537). Under the full shift both are near chance (DINOv2 0.442, CNN 0.395; target-calibrated recall at 5% 0.080 vs 0.051). Head-only domain randomization for DINOv2 did not help (full 0.436, clean 0.538): a frozen encoder's features are what the sensor shift degrades, and the head cannot undo that. Reading: a pretrained encoder is the right lever for viewpoint/lighting gaps; the binding constraint toward real cameras is sensor quality at this tiny resolution (the agent is ~4 px), so the next step is higher native resolution and/or fine-tuning the encoder with sensor-noise augmentation.",
 "infrastructure": "First attempt crashed with CUDA \"illegal instruction\" during DINOv2 extraction after the scratch CNN had finished (logged in target/vision-wm/infrastructure_failures.jsonl; no concurrent CUDA process; the RTX 4060 fault documented in this repo). Whole script rerun; scratch-CNN numbers reproduced within ~0.01."
